Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes, using structured mixed-radix packing and general-purpose fallbacks. The 44,267-byte corpus compresses to 16,776 bytes: 62.10% reduction, versus default zlib’s 22,390 bytes (49.42%). Verified byte-identical CLI restoration and 84 additional round trips. The registered assay, python3 assay.py, checks correctness, prints the required percentage, and runs in approximately 0.64 seconds.